    "request-time native file observations separated from manifest assertions",
    "64 filesystem checks, 8MiB per file, 32MiB total, at most64 path segments; unsupported/symlink/FIFO/budget/unreadable/unstable stay unchecked",
    "descriptor/path dev/ino/size/mtime/ctime validation; no promise of continued integrity after response",
    "shared facts reject mismatched manifest/revision/observation bindings; UI matrix no status-only pass",
    "existing eventId/seq/revision/path/digest history retained as recorded_assertion; currentVersion requires exact current plan revision; always explicitly incomplete because historical commits are non-atomic",
    "whole objective unchanged, no acceptance gate or creator attribution",
    "missing declarations never become current missing facts without bound native observation; pure metadata accessibility stays unchecked",
    "cross-identity selection uses immutable createdAt plus stable declaration order for same-clock ties, never mutable updatedAt/revision"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "original HTTP missing-file, same-artifact overwrite, native file drift counterexamples",
    "warm/cold/replay/restart metadata version equality",
    "real state-persist then append-event failure shows missing_current_event without sourceEventId",
    "wrong event path/run/thread and recomputed wrong snapshot plan/revision cannot bind",
    "same-byte content with changed plan revision does not reuse old current observation",
    "real same-size concurrent write with restoredmtime is unchecked",
    "no older-version fallback",
    "independent same-tick same-metadata reassertion state/event gap cannot reuse prior currentVersion",
    "a later unrelated plan revision removes current event binding but freshly matched bytes still pass integrity",
    "actual read return bytes remain <=8MiB per file and <=32MiB total even with real concurrent growth",
    "HTTP missing declaration followed by external reappearance with no new events yields observed/available, unknown integrity, missingCount0",
